    {
      "name": "BookingMonthView",
      "description": "The month: its title with arrows between months, the weekday names (read as full names), and a button per day at least 44 points (web, Apple) or 48 dp (Android) high with the day's spoken label; bookable days are outlined, booked days filled with the booked colour, the chosen day with the accent, closed days struck through, and only selectable days answer. Web MonthView inside a role grid of rows and gridcells; Swift BookingMonthView(grid:locale:statuses:booked:selected:months:style:labels:onSelect:onMonth:), whose days take the focus on Apple TV and grow when focused; Kotlin @Composable BookingMonthView(grid, locale, style, labels, onSelect, modifier, statuses, booked, selected, months, onMonth) with TalkBack descriptions, roles and selected states.",
